# Project language policy

- Apply project-wide. Read root AGENTS.md for the full required policy.
- Spanish is the complete default website language across public/admin, accessibility, errors, consent/help/privacy, explanations, metadata and exports.
- Keep Catalan, Basque and Galician interfaces in scope; activate each only after complete fluent-reviewed UI/question translations.
- All original code and developer documentation are English: identifiers, files, routes, schema/API keys, statuses/reason codes, comments, docblocks, tests and logs.
- Translation values and reviewed source/content data form the intentional content layer.
- Use English semantic keys with Spanish values in lang/es/*.php and approved regional catalogs in ca/gl/eu.
- Example: results.insufficient_evidence resolves to No hay suficiente evidencia para calcular un resultado. in Spanish.
- Browser UI consumes the approved local dictionary; long translated content stays outside scoring logic.
- Default/fallback locale is es; HTML language and formatting follow the selected approved locale. Keep the code/Eloquent pluralizer English.
- No unsupported English UI. Spanish runtime fallback must not justify launching incomplete regional translations.
- Localize framework/package UI and validation; never show raw exceptions, codes or unresolved keys.
- Preserve exact original quotations and official names; label reviewed translations separately.
- AI drafts public translations only; fluent reviewers approve them, particularly Basque and nuanced policy text.
- Require planned CI checks for hardcoded UI strings, enabled-locale key coverage, placeholders/plurals and unresolved keys.
- Use template/AST-aware checks and reviewed exceptions; enumerate dynamic translation mappings.
- Require language browser checks across public/admin and normal/empty/error flows plus accessibility and exports.
- Preserve question IDs, answer scales, evidence, weights and scores across locales.
- Review English naming and fluent translated copy separately; automated language detection is insufficient.
- Preserve private local matching when changing presentation.
- The local Laravel bootstrap exists; production language CI/browser checks and fluent-reviewed UI/question content remain implementation work.
